  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/tarball/v5.1.29",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/zipball/v5.1.29",
  "body": "**Child tasks and Kibitzer wakes of a fast-mode session no longer fail with `model_unavailable`: a `-fast` pin is accepted when the session starts on its paired base model.** Since 5.1.25, a category pinned to a `-fast` catalog variant such as `chatgpt-subscription/gpt-6-luna-fast` was refused after start, because senpi starts a `-fast` pin on its base model with the priority tier. Kibitzer recall wakes failed on every wake, and the built-in fast-first chains (`quick`, `deep-low`, `deep-high`, `ultrabrain`) silently skipped their first model. A run that started on the standard tier instead of priority is now accepted and recorded on the task (`effective_model.service_tier`) instead of refused. ([#9793](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/issues/9793), [#9808](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/pull/9808), [#9812](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/issues/9812), [#9813](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/pull/9813))\n\n**omo runs on senpi 2026.10.10-11.** `tool_schema(\"eval:environments\")` now documents `packages.install` and its `environment_install_timeout`, so JavaScript and Python cells can discover how to install packages without changing the default eval description or parameters. Julia, Ruby and Python cells do less fixed work per cell: no globals walk below the memory thresholds, no awaited cwd stat, and leaner Python queue and capture bookkeeping. A scheduled prompt created in a desktop thread before the OmO desktop moved that folder now fires, and `--session`, `--resume` and `--continue` find such sessions in the folder's new home. A session another live process already holds is refused with a typed `session_held` error instead of being opened twice. Sessions that share MCP servers but resolve different MCP configs no longer break each other's tools. A goal whose continuation stops also stops its timer. On Windows, stopping a command's process tree can no longer kill an unrelated process that reused a pid. On macOS and Linux, processes a JavaScript eval cell starts get their own process group, so a group kill can't stop the agent, and leftover grandchildren are stopped when the cell ends. Full engine notes: [senpi 2026.10.10-11](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/senpi/releases/tag/v2026.10.10-11). (code-yeongyu/senpi#3003, code-yeongyu/senpi#3028, code-yeongyu/senpi#3033, code-yeongyu/senpi#3034, code-yeongyu/senpi#2990, code-yeongyu/senpi#2951, code-yeongyu/senpi#2597, code-yeongyu/senpi#3007, code-yeongyu/senpi#2999, code-yeongyu/senpi#2995, code-yeongyu/senpi#3020, #9825)\n\n### Fixed\n\n**A background child no longer stays suspended while its parent is running.** A child parked while its parent session was still live was only revisited at the parent's next start, so it could sit suspended for hours and a goal waiting on its result waited forever. It is now revived right away, or ends with one result. ([#9350](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/issues/9350), [#9799](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/pull/9799))\n\n**omo.dev shows its live stats more reliably.** A cold page load whose first stats refresh hit one upstream blip showed the fallback numbers; it now falls back to the last complete set instead. ([#9820](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/issues/9820), [#9821](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/pull/9821))\n\n- 29fa016ac Merge pull request #9823 from code-yeongyu/docs/5.1.29-notes\n- a9562635a docs(changelog): 5.1.29 release notes (lead with the -fast fix; promote the -11 adoption entry from #9825)\n- 78214c8c6 Merge pull request #9826 from code-yeongyu/fix/get-worker-rollup-first-day\n- 3201f741b fix(get-worker): the hourly rollup never writes days before ROLLUP_FIRST_DAY (2026-10-10)\n- 8e750a6b6 Merge pull request #9822 from code-yeongyu/fix/first-deploy-asset-history\n- 06f3a39df Merge pull request #9819 from code-yeongyu/test/9766-stage2-guard-followups\n- dfc99dc5d fix(web): restore the workflow tests (committed empty); report the waiver only when used; cutover summary prints the reason\n- 4b5d0b8d6 Merge pull request #9816 from code-yeongyu/cutover/repoint-installer-mirror\n- f698f74f5 fix(web): first deploy after a deployment made outside the retention pipeline (dispatch-only reason)\n- efb8ca510 Merge pull request #9821 from code-yeongyu/fix/9820-stats-last-known-good\n- 0d14edbd4 style(web): prettier on the stats tests\n- 014d3591c test(web): stored copy keeps its age; malformed counts, description and time are ignored\n- 6be372286 fix(web): serve a shared last-known-good stats copy when a cold isolate refresh fails\n- ac9fcb6f4 Merge pull request #9815 from code-yeongyu/cutover/repoint-omo-deploys\n- cd2da6329 test(#9766): stage 2: list only omo-test-session-manager-fallback- (review)\n- cbeec581d test(#9766): stage 2: the shrink check accepts narrowing; list omo-test-session-manager- for omo-opencode\n- aaaccc383 Merge pull request #9818 from code-yeongyu/test/9812-fast-spelling-pin\n- c03993053 test(#9766): stage 2 review: both messages in the thrown error, two-way creator match, skip own fixtures\n- 2d43758ef test(#9766): stage 2: shared matcher with a table test, both errors from the hermetic-home teardown, derivation script, drop generic and duplicate entries\n- 5a1a127b5 Merge pull request #9813 from code-yeongyu/fix/9812-fast-pairing\n- 6ba3f19dc Merge pull request #9810 from code-yeongyu/fix/9766-test-temp-leak\n- 556e338d8 ci(installer): check the served channel against the bucket pointer after the run, with a bounded wait\n- 4bc6edfc3 ci(cutover): installer mirror writes the Sisyphus Labs omo-releases bucket and proves get.omo.dev serves the tag\n- 4038c65c3 ci(cutover): gate the manual omo-get deploy too, fail closed without a ledger or migrations, and update the deploy docs\n- bd42334f9 ci(cutover): live deploys target the Sisyphus Labs account; omo-get refuses a pending D1 migration\n- 6355b0842 test(#9766): exact report-only entr